#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Post a weekly digest of homelab project ideas to Discord (as Radagast).

Managed by Ansible (roles/cmd_center/tasks/scout.yml). Local edits are
overwritten.

Usage:
    lab-scout weekly [--dry-run]

weekly     Build an inventory of what the lab already runs from local git refs,
           ask claude (web search only) for candidate projects, validate and
           fact-check every candidate, and post at most LAB_SCOUT_MAX_IDEAS of
           them. Run by lab-scout.timer.
--dry-run  Everything except resolving the webhook and posting: prints the
           Discord payload as JSON, never touches 1Password, and writes no
           seen state and no metrics.

Facts are never taken from the model. Star counts, the last push date and the
license come from `gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>`; a non-GitHub link is only
checked to answer. The model is told not to state numbers, and text that
still carries one is dropped (lab-changelog #168: haiku merged two numbers
from a PR body into a false claim).

SECURITY: model output is shaped by fetched web content, so it is untrusted.
Every idea is validated and dropped (never repaired) when it breaks a rule,
every piece of text that reaches Discord goes through discord_text(), the
payload carries allowed_mentions {"parse": []}, links must be plain https to a
public host, and the webhook URL is never logged or put in an exception.

The webhook, logging, markdown escaping, lock and posting helpers mirror
files/lab-changelog on purpose, so each script stays self-contained. Keep
fixes to them in step.

Configuration (environment, all optional):
    LAB_SCOUT_OP_REFERENCE      1Password reference of the webhook URL
    LAB_SCOUT_OP_LIB_DIR        directory holding op-killswitch.sh and
                                op-secret-cache.sh
    LAB_SCOUT_OP_TOKEN_FILE     1Password service account token file
    LAB_SCOUT_STATE_DIR         seen state and lock directory (absolute)
    LAB_SCOUT_PROFILE           lab profile YAML passed to the model
    LAB_SCOUT_INVENTORY         repo:path,path;repo:path (path/* also lists
                                one level of subdirectories)
    LAB_SCOUT_EXTRA_INVENTORY   comma separated names the lab also runs
    LAB_SCOUT_METRICS_FILE      node_exporter textfile ("" disables metrics)
    LAB_SCOUT_CLAUDE_BIN        claude CLI path
    LAB_SCOUT_CLAUDE_MODEL      model alias (opus)
    LAB_SCOUT_CLAUDE_TIMEOUT    model call timeout in seconds (900)
    LAB_SCOUT_MAX_IDEAS         ideas posted per run (5, at most 10)
    LAB_SCOUT_MAX_STALE_DAYS    drop GitHub repos not pushed for longer (180)
    LAB_SCOUT_FETCH_DOMAINS     comma separated hosts WebFetch may read
    LAB_SCOUT_CONFIG            KEY=VALUE file holding any of the above
                                (/etc/default/lab-scout); the environment
                                wins over the file
"""

